1
00:00:02,218 --> 00:00:07,302
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,793 --> 00:00:09,859
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,715 --> 00:00:13,428
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:13,812 --> 00:00:19,089
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:19,163 --> 00:00:20,280
Dear brothers and sisters,

6
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,366
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته’

7
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:29,014
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he would leave to go Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

8
00:00:29,788 --> 00:00:36,050
he would appoint somebody behind to take care of the affairs of Madina and to take care of the affairs of his family.

9
00:00:36,545 --> 00:00:40,339
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ on this journey, the Battle of Tabook(تبوك),

10
00:00:41,053 --> 00:00:46,177
he appointed Muhammad Ibn Muslima(محمد ابن مسلمه) to be the Ameer(امير) over Madina

11
00:00:46,621 --> 00:00:51,721
and he appointed Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to take care of his family.

12
00:00:52,514 --> 00:00:56,877
Some of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) as usual they started spreading rumors around,

13
00:00:57,316 --> 00:01:00,887
how come Rasool Allah ﷺ left Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) behind.?

14
00:01:01,196 --> 00:01:02,437
They were saying; "اِسْتَثْقَلَهْ"

15
00:01:02,804 --> 00:01:06,955
The literal meaning is, he is heavy, meaning he is a burden

16
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:10,098
and that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ left him behind.

17
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:14,269
So Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him,

18
00:01:14,672 --> 00:01:16,482
I mean this is what people are saying and

19
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:21,653
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) wanted to go out obviously not to miss out on such as a Ghazwa(غزوة).

20
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:25,305
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

21
00:01:25,361 --> 00:01:32,630
یا علی : أمَا تَرْضَى أنْ تَكُونَ مِنِّي بمَنْزِلَةِ هَارُونَ، مِن مُوسَى، إِلَّا أنَّهُ لا نَبِيَّ بَعْدِي

22
00:01:32,966 --> 00:01:39,549
O Ali(علي) doesn't it please you to be to me, what Haroon(هارون) was to Musa(موسى).

23
00:01:40,025 --> 00:01:42,264
 Except that there is no Prophet after me.

24
00:01:42,614 --> 00:01:49,804
When Musa عليه السّلام went to speak to Allahعَزّوجَلّ, he left behind Haroon عليه السّلام

25
00:01:50,301 --> 00:01:53,339
and he appointed him to take care of the affairs of Bani Israel(بني اسرائيل).

26
00:01:53,723 --> 00:01:56,895
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and I'm doing the same to you.

27
00:01:56,965 --> 00:02:01,828
You are to me what Haroon(هارون) was to Musa عليه السّلام.

28
00:02:02,047 --> 00:02:05,483
Except that there's no Prophet after me because Haroon(هارون) was a Prophet.

29
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:09,251
So, this is one of the great virtues of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

30
00:02:09,318 --> 00:02:13,763
that we the people have Sunnah(سنة) believe in, obviously the Shia(شيعه) carry this too far.

31
00:02:14,207 --> 00:02:18,208
And based on it, what cannot be based on this Hadith(حديث),

32
00:02:18,571 --> 00:02:21,128
but we as Ahl-Us-Sunnah(اهل السنة) believe that

33
00:02:21,230 --> 00:02:25,101
Rasool Allah ﷺ did leave Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) behind and this is an authentic narration.

34
00:02:25,449 --> 00:02:31,017
And that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) held a special status with Rasool Allahصلوات الله وسلام عليه,

35
00:02:31,531 --> 00:02:32,942
and the army left.

36
00:02:33,188 --> 00:02:38,339
Some of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) were speaking among themselves and they said;

37
00:02:38,628 --> 00:02:43,436
Do you think that fighting the Romans is like Arabs fighting each other?

38
00:02:44,147 --> 00:02:47,714
You're going to come back tied in ropes.

39
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:53,050
Speaking such words in an army that's going out to meet an enemy is not good

40
00:02:53,225 --> 00:02:58,652
this is a demoralizing, it's not good to talk in such a way

41
00:02:58,732 --> 00:03:04,799
and put fear in the hearts of the soldiers and terrify them, about their enemy.

42
00:03:05,462 --> 00:03:12,467
And even though this conversation was private but  Allahعَزّوجَلّ exposed them to Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

43
00:03:12,899 --> 00:03:15,890
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) go to those men

44
00:03:16,231 --> 00:03:19,790
and ask them what they have said, because they have burned themselves.

45
00:03:19,830 --> 00:03:21,820
"اِحْتَرَقوْا اَدْرِكْهُمْ"

46
00:03:22,093 --> 00:03:25,736
Catch them because they have burned and ask them, what they have said.

47
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:31,919
If they do not admit it, tell them you have said so and so, you have said such and such.

48
00:03:32,622 --> 00:03:35,990
So, Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) went and told them that this is what you have said.

49
00:03:36,015 --> 00:03:38,232
They came back to Rasool Allah ﷺ apologizing.

50
00:03:39,137 --> 00:03:41,028
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية),

51
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:45,881
وَلَئِنْ سَأَلْتَهُمْ لَيَقُولُنَّ إِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوضُ وَنَلْعَبُ ۚ

52
00:03:45,905 --> 00:03:48,963
When they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, they said, O Rasool Ullah, we were just joking.

53
00:03:49,818 --> 00:03:50,967
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

54
00:03:51,096 --> 00:03:59,378
وَلَئِنْ سَأَلْتَهُمْ لَيَقُولُنَّ إِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوضُ وَنَلْعَبُ

55
00:03:59,717 --> 00:04:07,292
قُلْ أَبِاللَّهِ وَآيَاتِهِ وَرَسُولِهِ كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَهْزِئُونَ۝

56
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:13,434
لَا تَعْتَذِرُوا قَدْ كَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ إِيمَانِكُمْ

57
00:04:13,801 --> 00:04:21,527
إِنْ نَعْفُ عَنْ طَائِفَةٍ مِنْكُمْ نُعَذِّبْ

58
00:04:21,646 --> 00:04:28,729
 نُعَذِّبْ طَائِفَةً بِأَنَّهُمْ كَانُوا مُجْرِمِينَ۝

59
00:04:29,114 --> 00:04:35,198
And if you ask them, they will surely say we were only conversing and playing,

60
00:04:35,783 --> 00:04:43,024
say is it Allah and His verses and His messenger that you were mocking, make no excuse.

61
00:04:43,374 --> 00:04:48,233
You have disbelieved, after your belief, if you pardon one faction of you,

62
00:04:48,515 --> 00:04:51,435
we will punish another faction because they were criminals.

63
00:04:52,044 --> 00:04:55,323
And these are versus 65 and 66 of Surah Toubah(سورة التوبة).

64
00:04:55,609 --> 00:05:03,863
These Ayaat(آيات), make it clear that joking and mocking anything of religious value is Haram(حرام)

65
00:05:03,903 --> 00:05:06,062
and it can reach to the level of Kuffr(كفر).

66
00:05:06,426 --> 00:05:07,783
Because Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

67
00:05:08,014 --> 00:05:11,191
لَا تَعْتَذِرُوا قَدْ كَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ إِيمَانِكُمْ ۚ

68
00:05:11,429 --> 00:05:14,570
Make no excuse you have disbelieved after your belief.

69
00:05:15,011 --> 00:05:17,657
And if we look at it, what have they said,

70
00:05:18,118 --> 00:05:20,703
They just said that the Romans are going to defeat you.

71
00:05:21,379 --> 00:05:26,272
So, this tells us that mocking, making fun of anything in Islam,

72
00:05:26,714 --> 00:05:31,283
whether it is making fun of Qur'an, making fun of Hadith(حديث),

73
00:05:31,537 --> 00:05:40,472
making fun of Rasool Allah ﷺ or joking in a way that is disrespectful to the divinity of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

74
00:05:40,836 --> 00:05:46,207
All of this is very, very dangerous and it can lead to Kuffr(كفر) and it's a sign of Nifaaq(نفاق).

75
00:05:46,867 --> 00:05:50,183
So, we need to be very careful, and not make jokes and fun because

76
00:05:50,453 --> 00:05:52,563
sometimes there are jokes that are inappropriate,

77
00:05:53,145 --> 00:05:57,362
there are jokes that make fun of Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an or su'ar(سورۃ) of Qur'an

78
00:05:57,717 --> 00:06:02,467
this should be avoided because of the extreme danger in it, it's blasphemy.

79
00:06:02,858 --> 00:06:05,509
So, as a Muslim, we need to be very cautious.

80
00:06:05,827 --> 00:06:08,970
It also tells us that Islam is sacred

81
00:06:09,432 --> 00:06:14,982
and we have to hold it in high esteem and give it the sanctity that it deserves.

82
00:06:15,217 --> 00:06:20,161
We should not belittle our religion and we should not let anyone else belittle our religion.

83
00:06:20,985 --> 00:06:24,734
So, these stern warnings were to the Munafiqeen(منافقين),

84
00:06:25,043 --> 00:06:30,229
who're making fun of the Muslims and the abilities of the Muslims.

85
00:06:30,916 --> 00:06:36,259
And also today, if we could implement these meanings on our modern day,

86
00:06:36,342 --> 00:06:45,429
even if we are weak, or disunited, we should not spread rumors and words that weaken the Muslims.

87
00:06:45,951 --> 00:06:51,895
And we should not implant in the minds of the Muslims that your enemy is undefeatable

88
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:58,358
and that you are weak, and you have no hope and you have no future.

89
00:06:58,838 --> 00:07:03,313
All of this, things that we should we as Muslim should not involve in,

90
00:07:03,337 --> 00:07:07,163
and we need to uplift the Ummah(امة), we need to encourage the Ummah(امة),

91
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:09,337
we need to remind the Ummah(امة), that is,

92
00:07:09,615 --> 00:07:11,762
كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ

93
00:07:11,786 --> 00:07:15,450
You are the best nation that was brought forth to mankind,

94
00:07:15,719 --> 00:07:21,391
we need to remind the Ummah(امة) of its bright past and bright future also.

95
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:28,952
Because we do as Muslims have a bright future because the future belongs to the Muttaqeen(متقين).

96
00:07:29,001 --> 00:07:30,978
وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ

97
00:07:31,162 --> 00:07:33,656
The end belongs to the people of Taqwa(تقوى).

98
00:07:34,269 --> 00:07:41,240
So, we should not speak about the ability and the strength and the power of the Kuffaar(كفار)

99
00:07:41,559 --> 00:07:47,867
and the weakness and the disunity of the Muslims in a sense that demoralizes the Muslims

100
00:07:48,328 --> 00:07:51,510
 and makes them give up and accept the status quo.

101
00:07:52,062 --> 00:07:53,574
As a Muslims, we shouldn't do that.

102
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:58,234
Now, the army left and as we mentioned before,

103
00:07:58,682 --> 00:08:03,033
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Istanfaar(إستنفار) a general mobilization.

104
00:08:03,334 --> 00:08:07,177
Every Muslim everyone, who says, "لا اله الا الله" Needs to come out.

105
00:08:07,809 --> 00:08:09,994
The army left and there were some people who stayed behind.

106
00:08:10,813 --> 00:08:14,229
Now whenever they would come to Rasool Allah ﷺ and say

107
00:08:14,651 --> 00:08:17,864
so and so did not come Rasool Allah ﷺ would say;

108
00:08:18,214 --> 00:08:25,366
 دَعُوْه’ ، فَإِنْ يَكُنْ فِيْهِ خَيْرٌ فَسَيَلْحِقْهُ اللهُ تعالى بِكُمْ ، وَإِنْ كَانَ غَيْرَ ذَلِكْ فَقَدْ أَرَاحَكُمُ اللهُ مِنْه’

109
00:08:25,933 --> 00:08:31,012
Leave him alone, if there's any good in him, Allah will make him follow you.

110
00:08:31,431 --> 00:08:37,076
And if he is not, then Allahعَزّوجَلّ has given you relief from him.

111
00:08:37,994 --> 00:08:41,552
And then they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: Abu Dhar(ابوذر) is not with us.

112
00:08:41,889 --> 00:08:46,638
Rasool Allah ﷺ said the same thing, Leave him if there is any good in him, he would follow you

113
00:08:46,931 --> 00:08:50,183
and if not then Allah has relieved you from him.

114
00:08:50,703 --> 00:08:56,689
Abu Dhar(ابوذر) was following them but his camel was slow and when it slowed him down too much,

115
00:08:57,100 --> 00:09:01,399
he picked up his belongings and jumped off the camel and left.

116
00:09:02,693 --> 00:09:08,071
And Abu Dhar(ابوذر) was walking in the desert, with his belongings, in the heat of the desert.

117
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:14,040
And then the Muslims see in the horizon, this man appearing far away

118
00:09:14,465 --> 00:09:16,772
walking alone in the heat of the desert.

119
00:09:17,671 --> 00:09:23,716
They came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: O Rasool Ullah, there is a man following us, far away.

120
00:09:24,174 --> 00:09:26,206
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

121
00:09:26,277 --> 00:09:27,418
 "كُنْ اَبَازَرْ"

122
00:09:27,547 --> 00:09:28,924
Be Abu Dhar(ابو ذر).

123
00:09:29,789 --> 00:09:32,201
When the man approached, it was Abu Dhar(ابو ذر).

124
00:09:32,659 --> 00:09:35,853
So, they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: O Rasool Ullah, it is Abu Dhar(ابو ذر).

125
00:09:36,514 --> 00:09:38,732
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

126
00:09:39,113 --> 00:09:45,154
يَرْحَمَ اللهُ أَبَا ذَرْ ، يَمْشِيْ وَحْدَه’ ، وَيَمُوْتَ وَحْدَه’ ، وَيُبْعَثُ وَحْدَهْ

127
00:09:45,776 --> 00:09:50,895
May Allah have mercy on Abu Dhar(ابو ذر), he walks alone, will die alone,

128
00:09:51,258 --> 00:09:53,970
and will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment alone.

129
00:09:54,595 --> 00:09:56,579
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), the years passed,

130
00:09:56,754 --> 00:10:05,475
and Abu Dhar(ابوذر) was living in the time of the extreme wealth of the Muslims and the Muslim Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

131
00:10:05,824 --> 00:10:10,742
And Abu Dhar(ابوذر) was a man, who was brought up in the tough desert,

132
00:10:11,270 --> 00:10:16,223
who believed in Islam, in the early days, when things were still tough.

133
00:10:16,995 --> 00:10:22,972
Abu Dhar(ابوذر) accepted Islam, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was in Makkah, when the things were hard.

134
00:10:23,817 --> 00:10:27,236
And Abu Dhar(ابو ذر), his personality, his description was,

135
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:33,291
he was a very dark man, well built, huge and he was hot tempered.

136
00:10:34,022 --> 00:10:37,484
And he was very strict, he was a very strict man.

137
00:10:37,968 --> 00:10:44,061
And he was a Zahid(زاهد), he followed a strict form of austerity.

138
00:10:44,537 --> 00:10:50,292
And he had the belief that Muslims should not store wealth, and keep it.

139
00:10:51,012 --> 00:10:58,222
And that they should give their wealth to the needy, and in the causes of good.

140
00:10:59,023 --> 00:11:01,362
While the predominant view among the Muslims

141
00:11:01,387 --> 00:11:04,300
and this is the view that is adopted by the Ulema(علماء) is.

142
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:08,309
 If a person pays a Zakat(زكواة) of his money than the rest of his money is Halal(حلال)

143
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:13,159
and people can save money and can leave behind money.

144
00:11:13,183 --> 00:11:17,246
Otherwise, there would be no point in having laws of inheritance in Qur'an,

145
00:11:17,271 --> 00:11:18,744
if you're not going to leave anything behind,

146
00:11:19,103 --> 00:11:23,544
but Abu Dhar(ابوذر) used to follow this strict austerity

147
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:26,743
and he was not getting along with the authorities

148
00:11:26,767 --> 00:11:28,739
and it was not getting along with many people.

149
00:11:29,624 --> 00:11:31,568
He was in Ash-sham(الشام) in the time of Muawiya(معاويه).

150
00:11:31,592 --> 00:11:35,264
And Ash-sham(الشام) was the store of the wealth, that was where the wealth is.

151
00:11:35,651 --> 00:11:39,018
Ya'ani(يعني) because of the Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), with Romans

152
00:11:39,264 --> 00:11:42,841
and because of the land of Ash-sham(الشام) itself is very blessed land,

153
00:11:43,284 --> 00:11:47,855
the Muslims were becoming very wealthy over there and he was not happy with that.

154
00:11:48,362 --> 00:11:51,155
So, Muawiya(معاويه) sent a letter to the Khalifah(خليفه) Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

155
00:11:51,179 --> 00:11:55,350
because Muawiya(معاويه) was the governor of Ash-sham(الشام), he sent a letter to the Khalifah(خليفه) telling him

156
00:11:55,375 --> 00:11:57,710
لَقَدْ اَفْسَدَ علَىَّ اَبُوْ ذرْ اَلشَّامْ

157
00:11:58,117 --> 00:12:00,997
Abu Dhar(ابوذر) has ruined Ash-sham(الشام) for me.

158
00:12:01,593 --> 00:12:08,714
So, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) recalled Abu Dhar(ابوذر), and summoned him to come back to Madina.

159
00:12:08,777 --> 00:12:11,042
So, Abu Dhar(ابوذر) left Ash-Sham(الشام) and he came to Madina.

160
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,803
And Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) told him to stay in Madina.

161
00:12:14,311 --> 00:12:20,167
Abu Dhar(ابوذر) told Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), I want nothing to do with your Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), leave me alone.

162
00:12:20,837 --> 00:12:22,330
Allow me to go to Ar-Ribdah(الربداة),

163
00:12:23,005 --> 00:12:26,879
which was a very small village or town and middle of the desert.

164
00:12:27,349 --> 00:12:29,698
So, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) gave him permission.

165
00:12:29,738 --> 00:12:34,839
 I mean, he didn't even want to stay in Madina, he was totally against what he was seeing.

166
00:12:35,635 --> 00:12:40,257
So, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) gave him permission to go to Ar-Ribdah(الربداة), he went there,

167
00:12:40,534 --> 00:12:41,358
and that's where he lived.

168
00:12:41,827 --> 00:12:47,537
And Uthman(عثمان) told him that I'm going to give you some camels as provision for you.

169
00:12:47,759 --> 00:12:52,133
He said: I want nothing to do with them, I will survive on my own.

170
00:12:52,528 --> 00:12:54,998
And he just left without taking anything.

171
00:12:55,379 --> 00:13:00,844
And when he was on his deathbed, alone, in the middle of the desert,

172
00:13:01,673 --> 00:13:06,034
with no one but his wife and no servant, no neighbors, no friends, no one.

173
00:13:06,635 --> 00:13:11,081
And Abu Dhar(ابوذر), the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ, this great Sahabi(صحابي), the scholar

174
00:13:11,441 --> 00:13:15,034
he used to be a Mufti(مفتي) in the time of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), Umar(عمر) and Uthman(عثمان).

175
00:13:15,687 --> 00:13:19,998
And now he's living alone no students, no friends, no neighbors, nobody.

176
00:13:20,616 --> 00:13:21,693
And he's on his deathbed.

177
00:13:21,844 --> 00:13:23,772
So, his wife started weeping.

178
00:13:24,019 --> 00:13:25,446
He told her: Why are you crying?

179
00:13:25,626 --> 00:13:28,585
She said: How come? You don't want me to cry,

180
00:13:28,823 --> 00:13:33,549
when you are dying over here and I don't even have anything to use as your coffin.

181
00:13:34,023 --> 00:13:36,159
And I have no strength and ability to burry to you.

182
00:13:36,569 --> 00:13:37,046
He told her;

183
00:13:37,086 --> 00:13:38,497
اَبْشِرِيْ وَلَا تَبْكيْ

184
00:13:39,331 --> 00:13:47,194
Be happy and do not cry, because I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say, to a gathering that included me

185
00:13:47,654 --> 00:13:52,751
One of you, will die in Falah(فلاح), Falah(فلاح) is an empty land.

186
00:13:53,364 --> 00:13:58,942
And his burial will be witnessed by a group of believers, Mo'mineen(مؤمنين).

187
00:13:59,525 --> 00:14:03,316
And then Abu Dhar(ابوذر) said: And all of the people in that gathering died.

188
00:14:03,837 --> 00:14:05,728
And the only one left behind is me.

189
00:14:06,268 --> 00:14:08,349
And they have all died in Jam'ah(جماعة)

190
00:14:08,388 --> 00:14:13,689
They were all in a group, I'm the only one that fulfills this Hadith(حديث), dying alone.

191
00:14:14,009 --> 00:14:14,416
So,

192
00:14:14,543 --> 00:14:15,533
اَبْصِرِ الطَّرِيْقْ

193
00:14:15,710 --> 00:14:17,794
 Go and check out the road.

194
00:14:18,294 --> 00:14:23,358
She said: What road are you talking about, the Pilgrims have already left home,

195
00:14:23,666 --> 00:14:28,867
they're back in their homes and the roads are unused.

196
00:14:29,325 --> 00:14:33,302
So, probably this was an area, where pilgrims would pass through.

197
00:14:33,598 --> 00:14:36,871
But after that you rarely see anyone, but he told her to go out.

198
00:14:37,261 --> 00:14:42,326
So, she would go out spend some time watching, seeing if there's anybody showing up.

199
00:14:42,814 --> 00:14:44,996
And then she would go back and nurse him,

200
00:14:45,370 --> 00:14:52,720
until one day she saw a group of men riding on their camels coming from the horizon.

201
00:14:53,343 --> 00:14:54,049
كَالرَّخُمْ

202
00:14:54,367 --> 00:14:57,398
They were described as looking like vultures.

203
00:14:57,578 --> 00:14:59,426
Apparently she gave them that description,

204
00:14:59,466 --> 00:15:03,936
because probably if you're in a desert, and you see people coming from far away on camels,

205
00:15:04,197 --> 00:15:06,387
that's how they would look like, like vultures.

206
00:15:07,357 --> 00:15:11,601
So, she waved to them and they came to her and they told her,

207
00:15:12,324 --> 00:15:15,824
what do you want Amat Ullah(اَمة الله), O servant of Allah! What is it that, you need?

208
00:15:16,458 --> 00:15:21,069
She said: There's a man over here who's dying and I want you to take care of him.

209
00:15:21,489 --> 00:15:22,639
They said: Who is he?

210
00:15:22,806 --> 00:15:23,982
She said: Abu Dhar(ابوذر),

211
00:15:24,206 --> 00:15:26,132
they said: The companion of Rasool Ullah.

212
00:15:26,172 --> 00:15:27,134
She said: Yes.

213
00:15:27,338 --> 00:15:29,476
فَفَدَّوْهُ بِآبَائِهِمْ وَاُمَّهَاتِهِمْ

214
00:15:29,748 --> 00:15:32,376
They sacrifice their fathers and their mothers for him.

215
00:15:32,701 --> 00:15:36,399
They said: May our fathers and mothers be sacrificed for him.

216
00:15:36,572 --> 00:15:40,667
And they rushed to help Abu Dhar(ابوذر) and they came in,

217
00:15:41,095 --> 00:15:44,723
when he was lying down in his last moments and he told him, Abshiroo(أبشرو)

218
00:15:45,123 --> 00:15:51,300
I give you the glad tidings, Rasool Allah ﷺ told me that you will die in an empty land.

219
00:15:51,658 --> 00:15:55,367
And your burial will be witnessed by people, who were believers.

220
00:15:56,135 --> 00:16:04,380
And then he told them, if I or my wife had the garment that is suitable for me to use as a coffin,

221
00:16:04,475 --> 00:16:06,347
 I would've used it but I have nothing.

222
00:16:06,836 --> 00:16:08,616
Abu Dhar(ابوذر) was living with nothing.

223
00:16:08,886 --> 00:16:12,098
He was visited by Abu Musa(ابوموسى) once,

224
00:16:12,519 --> 00:16:16,614
and Abu Musa(ابوموسى) came and saw Abu Dhar(ابوذر) doing this housework.

225
00:16:17,089 --> 00:16:19,994
And he came in to help him and Abu Dhar(ابوذر) told him;

226
00:16:20,113 --> 00:16:20,966
إلَيْكَ عَنِّيْ

227
00:16:20,990 --> 00:16:22,167
Leave me alone.

228
00:16:22,319 --> 00:16:24,049
Abu Musa(ابوموسى) said: I'm your brother,

229
00:16:24,186 --> 00:16:26,033
Abu Dhar(ابوذر) told him you're not my brother,

230
00:16:26,336 --> 00:16:30,599
you used to be my brother before you assume positions of leadership.

231
00:16:31,377 --> 00:16:35,253
And he didn't even want to have anything to do with somebody, who was appointed as an Ameer(امير),

232
00:16:35,319 --> 00:16:38,372
you can see how strict Abu Dhar(ابوذر) was, in his Zuhad(زهد).

233
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:41,933
And this other visitor came and described Abu Dhar(ابوذر)

234
00:16:42,294 --> 00:16:48,381
as having an unkempt hair and very old garments, he is living a very difficult, hard life.

235
00:16:48,885 --> 00:16:54,755
So, now it's time for his Janazah(جنازه) and he doesn't even have anything to use as a coffin.

236
00:16:55,202 --> 00:17:01,217
And then he told them, he said: If I had anything or my wife had anything, I would have used it, but I don't have anything.

237
00:17:01,827 --> 00:17:08,328
And then he told them and I don't want anyone of you to give me a coffin

238
00:17:08,503 --> 00:17:13,543
if you have been an Ameer(امير) or a policeman or a postman.

239
00:17:14,131 --> 00:17:16,292
So, if you have been an Ameer(امير) working with the government,

240
00:17:17,064 --> 00:17:22,496
or a police officer or a postman I don't want you to give me anything.

241
00:17:23,184 --> 00:17:30,341
So, if there is anyone among you, who hasn't assumed these posts in the past, then he can give me a coffin.

242
00:17:30,887 --> 00:17:37,836
All of them have assumed these roles, one point of time, except one Ansaari(أنصاري)

243
00:17:38,366 --> 00:17:40,755
who was a young man among them, who didn't.

244
00:17:40,983 --> 00:17:46,252
And he said, I'm going to give you two garments that were made by my mother.

245
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:54,537
And he gave him that to use as his coffin, and Abu Dhar(ابوذر) died alone, and he was buried.

246
00:17:55,196 --> 00:17:56,793
And they prayed the Janazah(جنازه) on him.

247
00:17:57,295 --> 00:18:03,474
And this is the end of the life of one of the great Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

248
00:18:04,176 --> 00:18:10,078
Dear brothers or sisters, I mean, forget about following the way of Abu Dhar(ابوذر), no one of us could do that.

249
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,328
 But we talked about Abu Dhar(ابوذر),

250
00:18:12,702 --> 00:18:17,563
so that we can make a comparison with ourselves and see how miserable we are.

251
00:18:18,617 --> 00:18:25,133
I mean, the luxury we live in, the safety, the security, the wealth, the easiness of life.

252
00:18:25,773 --> 00:18:33,123
When we compare that to the way of Abu Dhar(ابوذر), who held on to the strict Zuhad(زهد) until he passed away,

253
00:18:33,726 --> 00:18:37,937
 it shows us the huge difference between us and him.

254
00:18:38,978 --> 00:18:43,600
And it makes us realize how unfortunate we are.

255
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:46,949
 We asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ to forgive us.

256
00:18:47,530 --> 00:18:54,068
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to guide us to the straight path and make us true believers.

257
00:18:55,216 --> 00:18:58,902
Another one of the Sahabah(صحابه), an Ansari(انصاري), a man from Al-Ansaar(ألانصار),

258
00:18:59,439 --> 00:19:00,485
his name is Abu Khaisamah(ابوخيثمة),

259
00:19:00,746 --> 00:19:03,742
when Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims left he was still in Madina.

260
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:07,821
He went back home and he has two Areesh(عريش),

261
00:19:07,861 --> 00:19:10,766
Areesh(عريش) is a hut made from tweaks.

262
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:14,746
And in summer when you pour this water on this hut,

263
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:19,452
it becomes very comfortable and cool inside because air can come through.

264
00:19:19,644 --> 00:19:22,814
And when it's soaked with water, it's natural air condition.

265
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:27,820
So, he had these two huts and there was one of his wives in each hut

266
00:19:28,258 --> 00:19:31,785
and they have prepared for him food and cold water.

267
00:19:31,842 --> 00:19:33,909
 So, he comes in and sees this.

268
00:19:34,129 --> 00:19:35,202
And then he says;

269
00:19:35,798 --> 00:19:42,792
رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ـ فِيْ الضَّحِّ (الشمس) وَالرِّيْحِ وَالْحَرْ، وَأبُوْ خَيْثَمَةْ فِيْ ظِلِّ بَارِدْ

270
00:19:42,990 --> 00:19:47,869
وَطَعَامِ مُهَيَّأ, وَاَمْرَأةٍ حَسَنَاءْ فِيْ مَالِهِ مُقِيْمَ؟ ؟!، مَا هَذَا بِالنَّصَف العدل،

271
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:55,718
ثٌمَّ قَالَ: وَاللهِ لَا أَدْخُلُ عَرِيْش وَاحَدَةٍ مِّنْكُمَا حَتَّى أَلْحَقَ بِرَسُوْلِ الله ـ صلى الله عليه وسلم ، فَهِيِّئَا لِيْ زَادًا

272
00:19:56,064 --> 00:20:01,574
He said: Rasool Allah ﷺ is in the hot weather and the wind

273
00:20:02,133 --> 00:20:06,572
and Abu Khaisamah(ابوخيثمة) is in a cool shade and a prepared food.

274
00:20:07,181 --> 00:20:10,786
And with beautiful wife, this is not fair.

275
00:20:11,241 --> 00:20:14,832
In the name of Allah, I'm not going to enter into any one of these huts,

276
00:20:15,370 --> 00:20:21,197
until I follow Rasool Allah ﷺ, so prepare my provisions.

277
00:20:21,296 --> 00:20:29,483
So, they prepared for him, his provisions and he pulled one of his camels, and he followed Rasool Allah ﷺ.

278
00:20:30,118 --> 00:20:33,092
 He only catched up with them when they were at Tabook(تبوك)

279
00:20:33,885 --> 00:20:37,227
and he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

280
00:20:37,449 --> 00:20:39,279
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

281
00:20:39,486 --> 00:20:41,298
أَوْلَى لَكَ يَا ابا الْخَيْثَمَه

282
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:46,857
And that's a warning from Rasool Allah ﷺ to Abu Khaisamah(ابوخيثمة).

283
00:20:47,167 --> 00:20:50,329
And then he told Rasool Allah ﷺ what happened,

284
00:20:50,559 --> 00:20:53,520
So Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دُعَا) for him.

285
00:20:53,873 --> 00:20:58,305
Dear brothers and sisters reflection on this story of Abu Khaisamah(ابوخيثمة)

286
00:20:58,643 --> 00:21:03,123
pretty much the way Abu Khaisamah(ابوخيثمة) saw things in Madina

287
00:21:04,172 --> 00:21:07,002
is how we are and we are even in a better situation.

288
00:21:07,809 --> 00:21:09,240
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

289
00:21:09,443 --> 00:21:14,701
لَا تَدْخُلُوا مَسَاكِنَ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ، إلَّا أَنْ تَكُونُوا بَاكِينَ

290
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:20,167
فَاِنْ لَمْ تَكُوْنُوْ بَاكِيْن فَلَا تَدْخُلُوْعَلَيْهِمْ ،( حَذَرًا)، أَنْ يُصِيبَكُمْ مِثْلُ ما أَصَابَهُمْ

291
00:21:20,934 --> 00:21:27,731
Do not enter the dwellings of the people, who transgressed against themselves,

292
00:21:28,169 --> 00:21:30,459
except if you are going to weep,

293
00:21:30,864 --> 00:21:34,451
 if you are not going to weep then do not enter their dwellings,

294
00:21:34,954 --> 00:21:39,006
lest the punishment that afflicted them, afflicts you.

295
00:21:40,072 --> 00:21:43,850
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them to just pour away the water that they got,

296
00:21:44,317 --> 00:21:48,150
and the dough that they made from that water, to feed it to the animals.

297
00:21:48,685 --> 00:21:54,918
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to have nothing to do with Samood(ثمود), or their land or their water.

298
00:21:55,271 --> 00:21:57,720
Nothing! And Rasool Allah ﷺ told us why?

299
00:21:57,906 --> 00:22:04,238
We should either take the reminder and the lesson and weep because of what happened to them.

300
00:22:04,601 --> 00:22:06,254
Otherwise, we should stay away

301
00:22:06,279 --> 00:22:09,116
because the punishment of Allah could befall us like it befell them.

302
00:22:10,062 --> 00:22:12,775
And what we learn from this is, that

303
00:22:12,815 --> 00:22:20,609
we should have no pride whatsoever with the so called civilizations of the past that were Mushrikeen(مشركين)

304
00:22:21,053 --> 00:22:22,725
and who were punished by Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

305
00:22:23,347 --> 00:22:30,389
How can we have pride in Babylon, and Firoun(فرعون) and all of these other Kuffar(كفار),

306
00:22:30,582 --> 00:22:32,546
when they were enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ?

307
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:40,053
How can we be proud with the pyramids or proud with the ruins of Babel(بابل)

308
00:22:40,103 --> 00:22:45,990
or the ruins that exist in other parts of the Muslim world, whether they are Roman or Greek or whatever,

309
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:50,204
when these were people who are Kuffar(كفار), who are enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

310
00:22:51,334 --> 00:22:57,528
It's very sad to see Muslims having pride in their Pre-Islamic history.

311
00:22:58,094 --> 00:23:00,908
And this is a plot by the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

312
00:23:01,019 --> 00:23:04,464
By the way, they have mentioned this in some of their writings,

313
00:23:04,882 --> 00:23:10,609
that we want to revive the pre Islamic history in order to attach the Muslims to it.

314
00:23:10,937 --> 00:23:14,887
And this would lessen their attachment to their Islamic history.

315
00:23:15,710 --> 00:23:17,837
We need to put things in the right perspective.

316
00:23:18,658 --> 00:23:24,131
These are the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and we should not visit their sites

317
00:23:24,515 --> 00:23:30,878
except if we are going to take the reminder from it and if it is going to soften our hearts

318
00:23:30,984 --> 00:23:35,526
and make us weep because of the fate that occurred to them

319
00:23:36,099 --> 00:23:39,655
because of the wrath of Allahعَزّوجَلّ on them because of their Kuffr(كفر).

320
00:23:40,582 --> 00:23:48,964
Nowadays, it is a shame to see some Muslims taking these photographs next to the mummy of Firaoun(فرعون),

321
00:23:49,004 --> 00:23:50,395
 while they're smiling and happy.

322
00:23:51,345 --> 00:23:57,923
It is a shame to see that some Muslims are going as far as even naming their sons Firaoun(فرعون),

323
00:23:58,281 --> 00:24:04,388
 having pride in that part of history to the extent that they would name their sons Firaoun(فرعون)

324
00:24:05,002 --> 00:24:10,350
and this is because of this reviving, and they called civilizations.

325
00:24:11,042 --> 00:24:18,259
And they call it civilizations in a good sense, when in reality they have no civilization at all.

326
00:24:19,191 --> 00:24:23,407
Rasool Allah ﷺ went to make Wudhuu(وضؤ) and he was very late for Salah(صلاة).

327
00:24:23,923 --> 00:24:29,320
So the Muslims made Iqamah(إقامه) and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) led the Salah(صلاة).

328
00:24:29,791 --> 00:24:33,435
Rasool Allah ﷺ catch them, while they were still in prayer.

329
00:24:34,053 --> 00:24:39,227
And Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) wanted to retreat but Rasool Allah ﷺ had him carry on

330
00:24:39,541 --> 00:24:42,695
and Rasool Allah ﷺ prayed behind Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف)

331
00:24:42,735 --> 00:24:47,327
that makes Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) the only Sahabi(صحابي), whom Rasool Allah ﷺ prayed behind him.

332
00:24:48,021 --> 00:24:51,643
And this is a great virtue for Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه.

333
00:24:52,721 --> 00:24:59,254
Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه, says, that in the middle of the night, during the Battle of Tabook(تبوك)

334
00:24:59,308 --> 00:25:06,359
I saw a torch so I followed it and I saw Rasool Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Umar(عمر)

335
00:25:06,975 --> 00:25:14,625
and Abdullah Zul Bajadain Al-Muzni(عبد الله ذوالبجادين ألمزني) has died and they have prepared his grave

336
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:18,587
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was the one, who descended into his grave,

337
00:25:19,053 --> 00:25:25,328
while Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عمر) were the ones, who were descending the body to Rasool Allah ﷺ

338
00:25:25,717 --> 00:25:28,346
and Rasool Allah was telling them bring down your brother

339
00:25:28,371 --> 00:25:33,602
and they were handing Rasool Allah ﷺ the body of Zulbajadain(ذوالبجادين).

340
00:25:33,976 --> 00:25:38,216
Zulbajadain(ذوالبجادين) was a very poor man, unknown, simple

341
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:46,113
and it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عمر) and Rasool Allah ﷺ himself, who were preparing his Janazah(جنازه)

342
00:25:46,464 --> 00:25:47,987
and Abdullah Bin Masood(عبد الله بن مسعود) was watching

343
00:25:48,408 --> 00:25:53,251
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ was the one, who put him with his own hands in the grave

344
00:25:53,678 --> 00:25:55,334
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

345
00:25:55,694 --> 00:25:59,474
اَللَّهُمَّ اِنِّيْ قَدْ اَمْسَيْتُ رَاضِيًّا عَنْهُ فَارض عَنْهُ

346
00:25:59,962 --> 00:26:06,554
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: O Allah I am pleased with him, so O Allah be pleased with him.

347
00:26:07,163 --> 00:26:09,277
Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه said;

348
00:26:09,867 --> 00:26:12,240
يَا لَيْتَنِيْ كُنْتُ صَاحِبَ الْحُفْرَهْ

349
00:26:12,656 --> 00:26:15,237
I wish that I was the one, in that grave.

350
00:26:15,966 --> 00:26:19,579
To have this blessing of Rasool Allah ﷺ making that Dua(دُعَا) for you

351
00:26:19,603 --> 00:26:24,736
and holding you with his hands and putting you in the grave is such a great blessing.

352
00:26:24,760 --> 00:26:27,166
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبد الله بن مسعود) said: I wish I was there.

353
00:26:27,981 --> 00:26:31,922
When the army reached to the land of Romans, Ash-Sham(الشام),

354
00:26:32,666 --> 00:26:38,000
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to Uqaidar(اُكَيدر), Domat Jandal(دومة الجندل),

355
00:26:38,829 --> 00:26:41,822
the king of Domat Jandal(دومة الجندل).

356
00:26:42,554 --> 00:26:48,427
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) to bring him to capture him and bring him.

357
00:26:49,213 --> 00:26:54,599
And Uqaidar(اُكَيدر) was living in a very strong fortress in Domat Jandal(دومة الجندل).

358
00:26:55,236 --> 00:26:59,333
So Rasool Allah ﷺ told Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), you would find him hunting bulls,

359
00:26:59,867 --> 00:27:03,285
you find him hunting, Uqaidar(اُكَيدر) used to go and hunt.

360
00:27:04,038 --> 00:27:08,447
And he would go out on horseback with a large group of his men

361
00:27:09,020 --> 00:27:14,745
and they'd travel and spend extended periods of time searching for the bulls.

362
00:27:14,769 --> 00:27:19,076
I mean, it wasn't an easy thing and he used to train his horses specifically for that.

363
00:27:19,971 --> 00:27:25,696
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), with a number of Muslims to capture him and bring him.

364
00:27:25,871 --> 00:27:29,040
 And it was a full moon night.

365
00:27:29,970 --> 00:27:36,677
And Uqaidar(اُكَيدر) was with his wife, on his roof, roof of his palace.

366
00:27:37,410 --> 00:27:45,245
And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), they saw the bulls come right to the gates of the fortress,

367
00:27:45,985 --> 00:27:52,949
and they were scratching their horns on the walls, or on the gates of the fort.

368
00:27:53,515 --> 00:27:56,071
And that is something unbelievable, they have never seen that before.

369
00:27:56,100 --> 00:28:03,086
I mean, he would have to travel long distance to find them and here they are, right next to him.

370
00:28:04,181 --> 00:28:07,052
So, his wife told him, Did you ever see anything like this?

371
00:28:07,092 --> 00:28:07,904
He said: Never.

372
00:28:08,435 --> 00:28:11,626
She said: Is this something that you could pass on?

373
00:28:11,666 --> 00:28:12,587
He said: No.

374
00:28:12,961 --> 00:28:16,492
And he immediately went down and told his servants to prepare his horses.

375
00:28:17,009 --> 00:28:21,055
And he took with him a few of his followers along with his brother,

376
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:26,456
and they rushed out of the fortress to hunt down these bulls.

377
00:28:26,847 --> 00:28:32,957
And they were routed by Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and they were surrounded

378
00:28:33,284 --> 00:28:36,116
and the brother of Uqaidar(اُكَيدر) fought and he was killed.

379
00:28:36,365 --> 00:28:38,848
And Uqaidar(اُكَيدر) and the rest surrendered.

380
00:28:39,180 --> 00:28:41,239
And they were captured by Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

381
00:28:41,676 --> 00:28:44,152
And they were brought to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

382
00:28:44,626 --> 00:28:49,050
he agreed to the terms of paying Jizyah(جزيه) and going back.

383
00:28:50,611 --> 00:28:53,073
There was no fighting that occurred.

384
00:28:53,605 --> 00:28:59,011
Because the Romans, when they heard about the advance of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

385
00:28:59,346 --> 00:29:02,417
Allah has put fear in their hearts.

386
00:29:02,708 --> 00:29:04,417
So, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) they didn't come forth,

387
00:29:04,837 --> 00:29:09,396
even though they had better preparation, large numbers, stronger weapons,

388
00:29:09,821 --> 00:29:13,407
but they were afraid to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ in actual battle,

389
00:29:14,015 --> 00:29:19,552
and therefore Rasool Allah ﷺ stayed there and waited for them, and nobody came.

390
00:29:20,075 --> 00:29:24,598
And Rasool Allah ﷺ during that time, he opened a few cities

391
00:29:25,038 --> 00:29:29,500
and made agreements with others, and took Jizyah(جزيه) from them.

392
00:29:30,392 --> 00:29:36,147
So, it was very successful Ghazwa(غزوة), even though no fighting was involved.

393
00:29:36,679 --> 00:29:40,584
It was very difficult it was a test for the Muslims as we have mentioned.

394
00:29:40,823 --> 00:29:42,003
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

395
00:29:42,216 --> 00:29:53,706
لَقَدْ تَابَ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنْصَارِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ

396
00:29:54,455 --> 00:29:59,858
الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِنْ بَعْدِ

397
00:30:00,296 --> 00:30:08,698
مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٍ مِنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ

398
00:30:08,952 --> 00:30:12,881
إِنَّهُ بِهِمْ رَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

399
00:30:13,129 --> 00:30:18,011
Allah has already forgiven the Prophet and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), and the Ansaar(أنْصَار),

400
00:30:18,441 --> 00:30:20,768
who followed him in the hour of difficulty.

401
00:30:21,081 --> 00:30:22,878
The hour of difficulty is, the Battle of Tabook(تبوك),

402
00:30:23,457 --> 00:30:29,375
after the hearts of a party of them had almost inclined to doubt, because of the difficulty,

403
00:30:29,978 --> 00:30:31,642
and then He forgave them.

404
00:30:31,769 --> 00:30:35,023
 Indeed, He was to them kind and merciful.

405
00:30:35,377 --> 00:30:38,999
So, now you can see that we're reaching into the closing chapters

406
00:30:39,039 --> 00:30:42,103
because forgiveness is something that comes towards the end.

407
00:30:42,633 --> 00:30:46,003
So Rasool Allah ﷺ is being told and the Muslims are being told

408
00:30:46,505 --> 00:30:52,045
that Allah has forgiven Rasool Ullah and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), and the Ansaar(أنْصَار),

409
00:30:52,263 --> 00:30:54,448
who followed him in the hour of difficulty.

410
00:30:54,822 --> 00:30:58,551
So, Allah has given them Toubah(توبه), and has accepted their Toubah(توبه)

411
00:30:58,919 --> 00:31:03,599
and this means that the end of the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ was approaching

412
00:31:03,916 --> 00:31:10,218
because that is something that we do towards the end of Ibadah(عبادة) is to ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ for Istaghfaar(إستغفار).

413
00:31:11,279 --> 00:31:20,817
When Rasool Allah ﷺ left from Madina initially, he was invited to pray in a Masjid(مسجد) that was newly built,

414
00:31:21,111 --> 00:31:27,650
 there were some people next to Madina, who built a new Masjid(مسجد), it was all done finished

415
00:31:28,320 --> 00:31:30,977
 and when Rasool Allah ﷺ was going to Tabook(تبوك),

416
00:31:31,013 --> 00:31:34,388
they told him we want you to come and bless the Masjid(مسجد) with a Salah(صلاة).

417
00:31:34,730 --> 00:31:36,076
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

418
00:31:36,254 --> 00:31:41,591
I am traveling at the moment when I come back In Sha Allah(إن شاءالله) I will pray in your Masjid(مسجد).

419
00:31:41,730 --> 00:31:43,191
 But now we're traveling.

420
00:31:43,707 --> 00:31:45,973
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was close to Madina,

421
00:31:46,340 --> 00:31:52,605
Rasool Allah ﷺ was informed about the true intentions of the people of this Masjid(مسجد).

422
00:31:53,076 --> 00:31:56,224
You see, there was a man called Abu Aamir Al-Fasiq(ابوعامر الفاسق),

423
00:31:56,712 --> 00:32:01,455
this man belong to Al-Khazraj(الخزرج) and he was a prominent member of the tribe.

424
00:32:02,404 --> 00:32:06,824
He was given the name Abu Aamir Ar-Rahib(ابو عامر الراهب) in the time of  Jahilliyah(جاهليه),

425
00:32:07,290 --> 00:32:12,470
because he was a believer in Allah and he used to worship Allah

426
00:32:13,229 --> 00:32:18,022
and he has learned from the people of the book and followed their religion

427
00:32:18,276 --> 00:32:23,053
and he was a very religious person, deeply devoted individual.

428
00:32:23,745 --> 00:32:30,691
But Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), When Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Madina, he was one of his worst enemies.

429
00:32:30,784 --> 00:32:36,024
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), you can see the irony here of this devote individual,

430
00:32:36,048 --> 00:32:42,447
a person who's deeply religious, you would expect him to be the closest to Islam,

431
00:32:42,537 --> 00:32:44,007
but Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) he was the furthest.

432
00:32:44,174 --> 00:32:48,856
You can also see the irony of Mushrikeen(مشركين), polytheists, they're becoming Muslim,

433
00:32:49,134 --> 00:32:51,806
while the Jews and the Christians who know about Allah

434
00:32:51,987 --> 00:32:54,767
and you would expect them to become Muslim, they didn't.

435
00:32:55,157 --> 00:33:02,175
So, he went to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) encouraging them to fight against the Muslims

436
00:33:02,199 --> 00:33:05,887
and he participated in the battles of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) against Muhammadﷺ.

437
00:33:05,911 --> 00:33:10,484
In fact, in the battle of Uhud(أحد) he was the one who dug holes, the traps

438
00:33:11,016 --> 00:33:16,943
in which Rasool Allah ﷺ, fell into one of them, which caused the teeth of Rasool Ullah to break

439
00:33:17,316 --> 00:33:22,380
and for some iron nails from his helmet to enter into His cheeks.

440
00:33:22,764 --> 00:33:27,157
This was caused because of Abu Aamir Al-Fasiq(ابوعامر الفاسق), his name was Abu Aamir Ar-Rahib(ابو عامر الراهب),

441
00:33:27,462 --> 00:33:31,996
Abu Aamir(ابوعامر), the priest, he was given that nickname because of his, him being religious.

442
00:33:32,314 --> 00:33:34,510
Rasool Allah ﷺ called him Abu Aamir Al-Fasiq(ابوعامر الفاسق),

443
00:33:34,535 --> 00:33:37,925
Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) the corrupt rather than the priest, the corrupt.

444
00:33:38,718 --> 00:33:42,799
When he saw that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were unsuccessful in their fight against Rasool Allah ﷺ,

445
00:33:43,139 --> 00:33:45,943
he went all the way to meet Heracul(هراقل), Heraculus,

446
00:33:46,573 --> 00:33:50,831
and he would ask him to send an army to invade Madina.

447
00:33:51,661 --> 00:33:55,861
He was promised by Heracul(هراقل) that he would be given assistance.

448
00:33:56,058 --> 00:34:02,218
And he used to send letters, Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) would send letters to some of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) in Madina,

449
00:34:02,781 --> 00:34:10,032
 promising them that I'm going to come with an army to destroy the Muslim state.

450
00:34:10,384 --> 00:34:19,528
And what happened was, he asked them to establish a base from which they can spread their conspiracy,

451
00:34:20,084 --> 00:34:26,488
 a place where they can meet and plot and that place was the Masjid(مسجد), they built.

452
00:34:26,735 --> 00:34:28,822
A Masjid(مسجد) gives them a good cover.

453
00:34:29,236 --> 00:34:32,974
But in reality, it was a place to plot against the Muslims.

454
00:34:33,277 --> 00:34:38,553
It was a place to promote the agenda of the Kuffar(كفار).

455
00:34:38,987 --> 00:34:44,220
Rasool Allah ﷺ was given Wahii(وحي), revelation that exposed this plan.

456
00:34:44,786 --> 00:34:50,298
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in verse 107 to 109 Surat Taubah(سورة التوبه).

457
00:34:50,568 --> 00:35:01,340
وَالَّذِينَ اتَّخَذُوا مَسْجِدًا ضِرَارًا وَكُفْرًا وَتَفْرِيقًا بَيْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ

458
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:11,480
وَتَفْرِيقًا بَيْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَإِرْصَادًا لِمَنْ حَارَبَ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ

459
00:35:12,004 --> 00:35:22,879
وَلَيَحْلِفُنَّ إِنْ أَرَدْنَا إِلَّا الْحُسْنَىٰ ۖ وَاللَّهُ يَشْهَدُ إِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ۝

460
00:35:23,602 --> 00:35:25,602
And there are those hypocrites,

461
00:35:25,912 --> 00:35:33,696
who took for themselves a mosque for causing harm, and disbelief and division among the believers

462
00:35:34,135 --> 00:35:40,068
and as a station for whoever had wared against Allah and His Messenger before.

463
00:35:40,587 --> 00:35:44,295
And they will surely swear, we intended only the best.

464
00:35:44,769 --> 00:35:48,184
And Allah testifies that indeed they are liars.

465
00:35:48,536 --> 00:36:01,011
لَا تَقُمْ فِيهِ أَبَدًا ۚ لَمَسْجِدٌ أُسِّسَ عَلَى التَّقْوَىٰ مِنْ أَوَّلِ يَوْمٍ أَحَقُّ أَنْ تَقُومَ فِيهِ

466
00:36:01,388 --> 00:36:10,989
فِيهِ رِجَالٌ يُحِبُّونَ أَنْ يَتَطَهَّرُوا ۚ وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُطَّهِّرِينَ۝

467
00:36:11,394 --> 00:36:14,539
Do not stand for prayer there, within it ever.

468
00:36:15,069 --> 00:36:20,832
A Mosque founded on righteousness from the first day is more worthy for you to stand in.

469
00:36:20,856 --> 00:36:22,500
This is referring to the Masjid(مسجد) of Al-Qubaa(القباء).

470
00:36:23,109 --> 00:36:28,862
Within it are men, who love to purify themselves and Allah loves those, who purify themselves.

471
00:36:28,887 --> 00:36:31,968
So, Allah is telling Rasool Allah ﷺ, we should not pray in this Masjid(مسجد).

472
00:36:32,298 --> 00:36:35,887
But you should pray in a Masjid that was established on Taqwa(تقوى) from the first day,

473
00:36:36,256 --> 00:36:39,767
and where there are believers, people who want to purify themselves.

474
00:36:40,603 --> 00:36:48,339
أَفَمَنْ أَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهُ عَلَىٰ تَقْوَىٰ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوَانٍ خَيْرٌ أ

475
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:57,076
خَيْرٌ أَمْ مَنْ أَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهُ عَلَىٰ شَفَا جُرُفٍ هَارٍ فَانْهَارَ بِهِ

476
00:36:57,635 --> 00:37:06,294
فَانْهَارَ بِهِ فِي نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

477
00:37:06,881 --> 00:37:11,564
Then is one, who laid the foundation of his building on righteousness

478
00:37:12,052 --> 00:37:15,465
with fear from Allah and seeking His approval better

479
00:37:15,758 --> 00:37:21,539
or one, who has laid the foundation of his building on the edge of a bank about to collapse.

480
00:37:21,922 --> 00:37:25,063
So, it collapsed with him into the fire of hell.

481
00:37:25,472 --> 00:37:28,066
And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.

482
00:37:28,397 --> 00:37:36,532
لَا يَزَالُ بُنْيَانُهُمُ الَّذِي بَنَوْا رِيبَةً فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ إِلَّا

483
00:37:36,985 --> 00:37:45,424
 إِلَّا أَنْ تَقَطَّعَ قُلُوبُهُمْ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

484
00:37:45,835 --> 00:37:51,291
Their building which they built, will not cease to be a cause of skepticism in their hearts

485
00:37:51,552 --> 00:37:55,828
until their hearts are stopped and Allah is Knowing and Wise.

486
00:37:56,373 --> 00:38:01,265
Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that the Masjid(مسجد) should be burned down to the ground.

487
00:38:01,611 --> 00:38:05,080
And that is what happened and the plot was exposed.

488
00:38:05,525 --> 00:38:11,150
Brothers and sisters, the story of Masjid-e-Dharar(مسجد الضرار) is a story of a Masjid(مسجد)

489
00:38:11,695 --> 00:38:15,670
that was established to promote Kuffr(كفر) rather than Eeman(ايمان).

490
00:38:16,044 --> 00:38:19,652
While the Masjid(مسجد) of Qubaa(قباء) and the Masjid(مسجد) of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Madina

491
00:38:19,899 --> 00:38:23,772
was a Masjid(مسجد) that was established from the first day to promote the truth.

492
00:38:24,168 --> 00:38:32,315
And therefore, any Masjid(مسجد) that is existing today to promote the agenda of the disbelievers is a Masjid(مسجد) of Dharaar(ضرار).

493
00:38:32,655 --> 00:38:39,312
And it is the same because Rasool Allah ﷺ was told by Allahعزَوجل.

494
00:38:39,506 --> 00:38:41,641
 "ضِرَارًا وَكُفْرًا"

495
00:38:42,164 --> 00:38:48,146
It is a Masjid(مسجد) that was built, Dharaar(ضرار) which is harm and disbelief.

496
00:38:48,704 --> 00:38:54,485
And this is something that occurs nowadays you find that there are Masajid(مساجد)

497
00:38:54,824 --> 00:38:57,254
that promote the agenda of the Kuffar(كفار).

498
00:38:57,735 --> 00:39:04,351
Rasool Allah ﷺ entered into Madina and he was greeted by the people, saying,

499
00:39:04,597 --> 00:39:07,461
طَلَعَ الْبَدْرُ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ ثَنِيَّاتِ الْوِدَاعِ

500
00:39:07,636 --> 00:39:10,429
 وَجَبَ الشُّكْرُ عَلَيْنَا مَا دَعَى لِلَّهِ دَاعِ

501
00:39:10,647 --> 00:39:14,941
Some historians mentioned that these words were said;

502
00:39:14,981 --> 00:39:18,021
When Rasool Allah ﷺ, made Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina,

503
00:39:18,148 --> 00:39:20,399
but Ibn Qayyim(ابن القيم) says that, that is incorrect,

504
00:39:20,626 --> 00:39:24,056
because Saniya Al-Widaa(ثنية الوداع) is to the north of Madina,

505
00:39:24,309 --> 00:39:28,393
and when Rasool Allah would come from Makkah, he would be coming from the south.

506
00:39:28,768 --> 00:39:33,151
Therefore, he says that this happened, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was coming back from Tabook(تبوك)

507
00:39:33,482 --> 00:39:35,610
and not when he made Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina.

508
00:39:36,204 --> 00:39:40,370
Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن القيم) then goes on to mention some lessons and benefits

509
00:39:40,789 --> 00:39:43,306
that can be derived from this Ghazwah(غزوة).

510
00:39:43,474 --> 00:39:46,312
There's one more incident that occurred in this Ghazwah(غزوة).

511
00:39:46,660 --> 00:39:49,705
And I would mention that in the lecture of its own,

512
00:39:49,990 --> 00:39:51,943
and that is the story of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب إبن مالك).

513
00:39:52,305 --> 00:39:54,394
So, we'll leave that In Sha Allah(إن شاءالله) to the next lecture.

514
00:39:54,641 --> 00:39:56,214
We'll talk about some of the benefits

515
00:39:56,644 --> 00:39:59,877
that were mentioned by Ibn Al-Qayyim(ابن قيم) in his book Zaad Al-Ma'ad(ذاد المعاد).

516
00:40:00,107 --> 00:40:00,813
He says;

517
00:40:00,898 --> 00:40:04,856
فَصَلْ: فِي الْاِشَارَةْ اِلَى بَعْضُ مَا تَضَمَّنَتْه’ هَذَا لْغَزُوْة مِنَ الْفِقْهِ وَالْفَوَائِدْ

518
00:40:05,245 --> 00:40:10,701
A chapter on some of the benefits, we can learn in this as Ghazwah(غزوة).

519
00:40:10,879 --> 00:40:11,529
He says;

520
00:40:11,570 --> 00:40:14,613
اِذَاسْتَنْفِرَالْاِمَامُ الْجَيْشَ لَزِمَهُمُ النَّفِيْرَ

521
00:40:14,994 --> 00:40:21,709
If the Imam(اِمَام) mobilizes the army, then it is a must on them to respond.

522
00:40:22,185 --> 00:40:23,264
And he says;

523
00:40:23,306 --> 00:40:29,247
اِنَّ الْاِمَامَ اِذَاسْتَنْفَرَالْجَيْشَ، لَزِمَهُمُ النَّفِيْر، وَلَمْ يَجُزْلِاَحَدٍ التَّخَلُّفْ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهْ

524
00:40:29,578 --> 00:40:32,875
If the Imam(اِمَام) mobilizes the army,

525
00:40:33,207 --> 00:40:37,899
than it is mandatory on them to come and no one can stay behind.

526
00:40:38,302 --> 00:40:41,425
وَلَا يَشْتَرِطْ فِيْ وُجُوْبِ النَّفِيْر تَعْيِيْنُ كُلُّ وَاحِدْ

527
00:40:41,906 --> 00:40:47,675
And he says that a general mobilization is sufficient to make it obligatory,

528
00:40:47,699 --> 00:40:50,858
he doesn't have to mention each one by name.

529
00:40:51,286 --> 00:40:52,230
And then he says;

530
00:40:52,308 --> 00:40:56,238
وَهَذَا اَحَدٌ الْمَوَاضِعِ الثَّلَاثَةْ اَلَّتِيْ يَصِيْرَ فِيْهَا الْجِهَادُ فَرْضِ عَيْنَ

531
00:40:56,591 --> 00:41:01,774
And this is one of the three situations where Jihad(جهاد) becomes mandatory.

532
00:41:02,347 --> 00:41:05,658
He said: The second is when the enemy invades the Muslim land

533
00:41:05,690 --> 00:41:08,123
and the third is when the two armies meet.

534
00:41:08,615 --> 00:41:09,975
The next benefit,

535
00:41:10,085 --> 00:41:11,704
وُجُوْبُ الْجِهَادِ بِالْمَالْ

536
00:41:12,073 --> 00:41:17,632
It is mandatory to support fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) with wealth.

537
00:41:18,069 --> 00:41:18,666
He says;

538
00:41:18,714 --> 00:41:25,376
وُجُوْبُ الْجِهَادِ بِالْمَالْ كَمَا يَجِبُ بِالنَّفْسِ وَهَذَا اَحْدِيْ الرَّوَايَتَيْنْ عَنْ اَحْمَدْ، وَهِيَّ الصَّوَابْ اَلَّذِيْ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ

539
00:41:25,620 --> 00:41:29,296
And he said, and this is one of the two narrations from Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) and he said;

540
00:41:29,489 --> 00:41:35,727
there is no doubt in this, that it is mandatory to support fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) with your wealth.

541
00:41:35,998 --> 00:41:39,330
And he says that it is more important than fighting with yourself.

542
00:41:39,924 --> 00:41:45,573
جِهَادْ بِالْمَالْ شَقِيْقُ الْاَمْرِ وَاَهَمْ وَآكَدْ مِنَ الْجِهَادِ النَّفْسْ

543
00:41:46,473 --> 00:41:48,784
And then he mentions the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

544
00:41:48,822 --> 00:41:51,882
whoever finances a fighter than he has fought.

545
00:41:52,227 --> 00:41:58,411
And he goes to mention that whoever has financial ability, then that is what he should do.

546
00:41:58,771 --> 00:42:01,751
لَا يُعْذَرْ اَنْ الّعَاجِزْ بِمَالِهَ حَتَّى يَبْذُلَ جُهْدَهْ

547
00:42:02,147 --> 00:42:09,221
He said: The one who is incapable of fighting is not excuse, until he does his best.

548
00:42:09,972 --> 00:42:13,607
Because he said that the ones who stayed behind, they tried their best

549
00:42:13,645 --> 00:42:20,489
 they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, they said support us, finance us, we want to go out and they were eagerly trying to do so.

550
00:42:20,774 --> 00:42:24,221
Because when they were told that Rasool Ullah has nothing to support you with,

551
00:42:24,245 --> 00:42:26,290
they left with tears flowing from his eyes.

552
00:42:26,488 --> 00:42:29,322
So, he said that you need to do your best.

553
00:42:30,068 --> 00:42:34,025
لَا يَجُوْزُ الشُّرْبُ،وَلَا الطبخ ، وَلَاالْعَجْنُ ، وَلَاالطَّهَارَةْ ، مِنَ الْآبَارَ الثَّمُوْدْ

554
00:42:34,049 --> 00:42:38,151
He said: It is not allowed to drink or cook or prepare the dough

555
00:42:38,533 --> 00:42:41,879
or make Wadhoo(وضؤ) from the wells of the Samood(ثمود).

556
00:42:42,395 --> 00:42:47,028
And he said, that the reason is, and he mentioned it in another situation.

557
00:42:47,367 --> 00:42:51,994
It is because they are people whom Allah has incurred His wrath upon.

558
00:42:52,851 --> 00:42:56,842
وَمِنْهَا اَنَّ مَنْ مَرَّ بِدِيَارِ الْمَغْضُوْبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَالْمُعَذِّبِيْنَ

559
00:42:57,202 --> 00:43:06,112
لَمْ يَنْبَغِ لَه’ اَنْ يَدْخُلَهَا وَلَا يُقِيْمُ بِهَا، بَلْ يُسْرِعْ اُلسَّيْرْ، وَيَتَقَنَّعْ بِثَوْبِهِ حَتَّى يُجَاوِزْهَا

560
00:43:06,436 --> 00:43:11,701
He says: When you pass next to the places or the dwellings of the people

561
00:43:12,018 --> 00:43:16,247
whom Allah has punished, then you should not enter it and you should not stay there,

562
00:43:16,600 --> 00:43:20,960
and you should try to pass by it as fast as possible,

563
00:43:21,305 --> 00:43:25,595
and you should cover your face with your clothes until you pass it by.

564
00:43:26,064 --> 00:43:28,300
I mean, you should try to avoid it, as much as possible.

565
00:43:28,774 --> 00:43:33,514
Except if you are going to enter it crying, and you learn the lessons.

566
00:43:34,854 --> 00:43:37,084
جَوَازُ الْجَمْعَ بَيْنَ الصَّلَاتَيْنَ فِيْ السَّفَرْ

567
00:43:37,124 --> 00:43:40,261
It is allowed to combine prayers in travel

568
00:43:40,285 --> 00:43:44,716
because Rasool Allah ﷺ combined, when he was going to Tabook(تبوك).

569
00:43:45,296 --> 00:43:50,673
اِذَا بَعَثَ الْاِمَامُ سَرِيَةً فَغَنِمَتْ كَانَ مَا حَصَلَ مِنْ ذَالِكَ لَهَا بَعْدَ تَخْمِيْسَهْ

570
00:43:50,982 --> 00:43:54,937
If the Imam(اِمَام) sends, if the leader of the army sends a small group

571
00:43:55,757 --> 00:44:02,168
and they have won some spoils of war, then what they have won is belongs to them,

572
00:44:02,528 --> 00:44:06,299
after they give 20% of it, to the Ameer(أمير) of the Muslims,

573
00:44:06,701 --> 00:44:08,507
according to the rules of Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

574
00:44:09,052 --> 00:44:11,840
So, he says that it is not distributed among all of the army

575
00:44:11,865 --> 00:44:15,190
but it is given to the ones, who were sent out.

576
00:44:16,095 --> 00:44:18,684
فَصَلْ تحْرِيْقَ وَاَمْكِنَةِ الْمَعْصِيَّةِ وَهَدْمِهَا

577
00:44:18,928 --> 00:44:22,060
Places of sin should be burned down.

578
00:44:22,100 --> 00:44:26,734
And the evidence for that is what Rasool Allah ﷺ did with the Masjid(مسجد) Of Dharrar(ضرار).

579
00:44:26,759 --> 00:44:30,446
He said: This is a Masjid(مسجد) where people are going to pray and mentioned the name of Allah.

580
00:44:30,470 --> 00:44:34,395
Nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahabah(صحابه) to burn it, to the ground.

581
00:44:34,883 --> 00:44:37,328
He said: What about the places of sin?

582
00:44:38,007 --> 00:44:44,679
And he mentions like the places of prostitution and where alcohol is being sold.

583
00:44:45,034 --> 00:44:46,227
And he gives them example.

584
00:44:46,267 --> 00:44:52,279
He says, that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) has ordered that a village be burned down because they were selling alcohol.

585
00:44:53,170 --> 00:44:58,676
So, these are some of the lessons that Ibn Qayyim(إبن القيم) has mentioned, from Ghazwa-e-Tabook(غزوة التبوك).

586
00:44:58,701 --> 00:45:04,529
In sha Allah Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى) In our next session we'll talk about the story of Ka'ab Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه.

587
00:45:04,735 --> 00:45:07,761
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

588
00:45:08,071 --> 00:45:09,968
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

